    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> in 1815 and ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#dutch">Dutch</a> kings until 1890, it lost its western half to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#belgium">Belgium</a> in 1839.</li><li>Iron ore and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#steel">steel</a>, then banking and investment funds, made a poor farming country one of the richest in the world per head.</li><li>Occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#germany">Germany</a> in both world wars, it abandoned neutrality and became a founding member and seat of European institutions.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Schengen Agreement that abolished border checks across much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a> is named after a small wine-growing village in Luxembourg, where it was signed on a boat on the Moselle in 1985.</p></aside>
    </section>

